// Probe 04 — Cluster I variant: field-access text `??` "fallback"
//
// Tests whether the cluster I shape is LHS-shape-independent.  The LHS
// here is `obj.name` (a field read on a struct), still non-trivial in
// the parser's view, so the `_ncc_N` block is constructed.
//
// If 04 fails identically to 02, the cluster is "any non-trivial LHS,"
// confirming the diagnosis at PROBLEMS.md @P383 isn't vector-specific.
// If 04 passes while 02 fails, there's a vector-index-specific code path
// to investigate separately.
//
// Expected (rustc 1.96 / macOS): FAIL on --interpret, PASS on --native.
// Pairing: diff against probe 02 to confirm shape independence.
// Status: cluster I variant probe.

struct Holder { name: text }

fn main() {
  obj = Holder { name: "present" };
  a = obj.name ?? "fallback";
  assert(a == "present", "probe 04: got '{a}', want 'present'");
  println("probe 04 PASSED");
}
